From: EglantinePS5
Subject: up: a rejected compute program is thrown again straight from its stored error (EDEN_UP_COMPUTE_REJECT_FAST), off by default

What: once the lowering rejects a native compute program, every later dispatch of it went
RethrowIfRejected (throw 1, under the rejection lock) -> catch -> RememberRejection (lock,
std::current_exception, an emplace that keeps the old entry, two atomic stores) -> throw; (throw 2).
Ocarina rejects some compute programs (texture gather mode, per-tap gather proof, tensor settings)
and dispatches them again and again. With EDEN_UP_COMPUTE_REJECT_FAST=1 ComputeShader looks the
address up once and std::rethrow_exception's the stored error: one throw, no catch, no new
exception_ptr. RememberRejection returns at once for an address already recorded (the non-native
graphics path still rethrows and remembers per draw).

Not like #197: upstream returns nullptr and lets DispatchCompute throw a new "Native compute
pipeline unavailable". In this tree KeplerCompute::DispatchNativeCompute reads the error's text
("matrix multiply" sends it to the upscale stand-in), so that would change what is drawn. Here the
same error object comes out of the same calls (CurrentComputePipeline, or CurrentComputeNativeKey
with EDEN_NX2_OOT_SKIP_AA), so only the cost changes. Also one throw, like upstream. The OpenGL hunk
of #197 is not needed for the same reason. One race-only difference: off, a write that drops the
rejection between the rethrow and RememberRejection had it put back; on, it stays dropped and the
next dispatch lowers the program again (as for any written program).

Switch: EDEN_UP_COMPUTE_REJECT_FAST=1 (exact "1"), read once at the first compute dispatch that is
not cached. Off: one static bool tested in ComputeShader and RememberRejection, code as before.
Log (LOG_INFO, HW_GPU): "EDEN_UP_COMPUTE_REJECT_FAST on" once, then "EDEN_UP_COMPUTE_REJECT_FAST
fast_rejections=N steady_ms= last=<address>" at the 1st, 10th, 100th, ... fast-path dispatch (two
lines give the rate). No line after "on": the path is not reached (no rejected compute program).

Origin and credit: zortos293/Lichii #197 (809fb3aa35, Andre Saddler), adapted as above. The
draw-side twin (already ours) was "~1-2% of the GPU thread"; no fps number for compute.
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/shader_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/shader_cache.cpp
index 638d465..fdad74b 100644
--- a/src/video_core/shader_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/shader_cache.cpp
@@ -5,6 +5,9 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
 
 #include <algorithm>
+#include <atomic>
+#include <chrono>
+#include <exception>
 #include <cstring>
 #include <functional>
 #include <string>
@@ -35,6 +38,42 @@
 
 namespace VideoCommon {
 
+namespace {
+// EDEN_UP_COMPUTE_REJECT_FAST=1 (zortos293/Lichii #197, Andre Saddler): a compute program the
+// lowering already rejected is thrown again straight from the stored error (one throw) instead
+// of rethrown, caught, remembered again and rethrown (two throws, a locked insert and a
+// current_exception per dispatch); RememberRejection keeps the first error for an address.
+// Read once; anything but exact "1" is off, and off runs the code as before.
+bool ComputeRejectFast() {
+    static const bool on = [] {
+        const bool value = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_COMPUTE_REJECT_FAST");
+        if (value) {
+            LOG_INFO(HW_GPU, "EDEN_UP_COMPUTE_REJECT_FAST on");
+        }
+        return value;
+    }();
+    return on;
+}
+
+/// EDEN_UP_COMPUTE_REJECT_FAST: counts dispatches that took the fast path and logs the 1st, 10th,
+/// 100th, ... (with the time, so a rate can be read off two lines).
+void CountFastComputeRejection(VAddr addr) {
+    static std::atomic<u64> count{};
+    const u64 n = count.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed) + 1;
+    u64 mark = 1;
+    while (mark < n && mark <= (~u64{0}) / 10) {
+        mark *= 10;
+    }
+    if (mark == n) {
+        const auto ms = std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::milliseconds>(
+                            std::chrono::steady_clock::now().time_since_epoch())
+                            .count();
+        LOG_INFO(HW_GPU, "EDEN_UP_COMPUTE_REJECT_FAST fast_rejections={} steady_ms={} last={:#x}",
+                 n, ms, addr);
+    }
+}
+} // Anonymous namespace
+
 bool CanonicalKeys() {
     static const bool enabled = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_CANONICAL_KEYS");
     return enabled;
@@ -236,6 +275,24 @@ const ShaderInfo* ShaderCache::ComputeShader() {
     if (const ShaderInfo* const shader = TryGet(*cpu_shader_addr)) {
         return shader;
     }
+    if (ComputeRejectFast()) {
+        // The same error object the path below rethrows, along the same callers (KeplerCompute
+        // reads its text: "matrix multiply" picks the upscale stand-in), so only the cost changes.
+        // #197 returns nullptr here instead; in this tree that would turn the error's text into
+        // "Native compute pipeline unavailable" and lose the stand-in.
+        std::exception_ptr rejected;
+        {
+            std::scoped_lock lock{rejected_mutex};
+            if (const auto it = rejected_native.find(*cpu_shader_addr);
+                it != rejected_native.end()) {
+                rejected = it->second;
+            }
+        }
+        if (rejected) {
+            CountFastComputeRejection(*cpu_shader_addr);
+            std::rethrow_exception(rejected);
+        }
+    }
     try {
         RethrowIfRejected(*cpu_shader_addr);
         ComputeEnvironment env{*kepler_compute, *gpu_memory, program_base, qmd.program_start};
@@ -260,6 +317,12 @@ bool ShaderCache::IsRejected(VAddr addr) {
 
 void ShaderCache::RememberRejection(VAddr addr) {
     std::scoped_lock lock{rejected_mutex};
+    if (ComputeRejectFast() && rejected_native.contains(addr)) {
+        // #197: called from a catch block; the first error stays (emplace would keep it too),
+        // without capturing a new exception_ptr. The bounds below never shrink, so they already
+        // hold addr.
+        return;
+    }
     rejected_native.emplace(addr, std::current_exception());
     rejected_lowest.store((std::min)(rejected_lowest.load(std::memory_order_relaxed), addr),
                           std::memory_order_relaxed);
